Subject: [PATCH] KMSDRM: never request async page flips

The Rockchip VOP (RK3326 and friends) reports DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP, but
drmModePageFlip() with DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC returns EINVAL.  SDL then
logs "Could not queue pageflip: -22" every frame, never waits for vblank and
the program falls back to audio pacing, while SDL does a blocking modeset for
every presented frame (measured ~1946 failures in 30 s on an RG351V).

Only ask for async flips on hardware that actually accepts them.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
@@
-    viddata->async_pageflip_support = async_pageflip ? SDL_TRUE : SDL_FALSE;
+    /* Rockchip VOP: the kernel advertises DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP but rejects
+       DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC with EINVAL, which makes every frame fall back
+       to a blocking modeset.  Never ask for async flips there. */
+    (void)async_pageflip;
+    viddata->async_pageflip_support = SDL_FALSE;
